The CSSgrid-template-areasis a 
grid container property, and it specifies 
areas within the grid layout.

You can name grid items by using the CSSgrid-areaproperty, and then reference to the name in thegrid-template-areasproperty.

Each area is defined within apostrophes. The named grid items in each area is defined inside the apostrophes, separated by a space.

We can use a period sign (.) to refer to a grid item with no name:

To define two rows (two areas), define the second row inside another set of apostrophes:

Here, we will name all grid items to make a ready-to-use webpage template:

### Code Snippets

```
.container {
display: grid;
grid-template-areas: 'myHeader 
  myHeader myHeader myHeader myHeader';
}
.item1 {
grid-area: 
  myHeader;
}

---

.container {
display: grid;
grid-template-areas: 'myHeader 
  myHeader myHeader . .';
}
.item1 {
grid-area: 
  myHeader;
}

---

.container {
display: grid;
grid-template-areas:
'myHeader 
  myHeader 
  . . .'
'myHeader myHeader . . .';
}
.item1 {
grid-area: 
  myHeader;
}

---

.item1 { grid-area: header; }
.item2 { grid-area: menu; }
.item3 { 
  grid-area: main; }
.item4 { grid-area: right; }
.item5 { grid-area: 
  footer; }
.container {
display: grid;
grid-template-areas:
'header header header header header header'
'menu main 
  main main main right'
'menu footer footer footer footer 
  footer';
}
```
